        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: క్షతగాత్రులు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "క్షతగాత్రులు — kṣatagātrulu — \"the injured\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "క్షతగాత్రులను ఆసుపత్రికి తీసుకెళ్ళారు. kṣatagātrulanu āsupatriki tīsukeḷḷāru. The injured were taken to hospital."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A news word, nearly only in the plural: క్షత, wounded, and గాత్ర, the body. At the hospital the క్షతగాత్రులు (kṣatagātrulu) are given ఔషధం."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "క్షతగాత్రులు (kṣatagātrulu) is borrowed from Sanskrit: kṣata, \"wounded\" (CDIAL 3645), and gātra, \"a limb, the body\" (CDIAL 4124): those wounded in body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
